  {
   "id": "new_muslim_faq.faq.007",
   "kind": "faq",
   "stage": ["question"],
   "text": {
    "en": "What breaks wudu? Scholars agree on what comes out of the front or back passage, such as urine, stool and wind, and on deep sleep or fainting. Scholars differ on light sleep while sitting, bleeding, vomiting and touching: the Hanafi, Maliki, Shafi'i and Hanbali schools each hold their own view. Doubt alone does not break wudu."
   },
   "ageBand": ["adult", "13-17"],
